  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved access and provision of lifesaving interventions on health, nutrition and child protection in the most vulnerable communities and institutions in Bolivar and Sucre</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to improve access and provision of life-saving interventions on health, nutrition, and child protection in the most vulnerable communities in Bolivar and Sucre. This UNICEF project provides reproductive health (RH) interventions in the context of the Minimum Initial Service Package (MISP), including essential RH drugs and supplies and emergency obstetric care, and training of health staff on the Comprehensive management of Obstetric &amp; Pediatric Emergencies and Neonatal Care. The project provides life-saving assistance to 38,723 people, including 12,862 women, 2,749 men, 23,112 children, and 765 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
